# promise: #527
# A tab's name showed by the pointer over the page, now and then, with the sidebar hidden (#527). The
# sidebar's spaces sit side by side on a strip, and the hidden sidebar is parked just past the window's
# left edge, so the next space's tab list lies under the left of the page, as it does beside a shown
# sidebar. A view doesn't clip what it holds unless it says so (macOS 14), and AppKit doesn't cut a
# visible rect to a superview that doesn't, so that list's tracking area reached over the page: a
# pointer resting there hovered one of its rows, and its tip came up by the pointer. Only the space
# shown takes the pointer.
budget rss=700 stalls50=20
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "showToolbar": false}
